- How would you test durability during partial outages and ensure no data loss?
- What metrics indicate freshness and how would you alert on drift?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to implement cross-service consistency guarantees and reason about end-to-end latency under load.

## Key Concepts

- transactional outbox across DB and event bus
- idempotent producers and deduplication
- cache invalidation vs cache warmth
- end-to-end validation under peak load

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: transactional outbox pattern
async function commitUpdate(userId, pref) {
  await db.begin();
  await db.run('UPDATE users SET pref=? WHERE id=?', pref, userId);
  await db.run('INSERT INTO outbox (user_id, event_type, payload, processed) VALUES (?,?,?,false)', userId, 'pref_updated', JSON.stringify({pref}));
  await kafkaProducer.send({ topic: 'user.events', key: String(userId), value: JSON.stringify({userId, pref, ts: Date.now()}) });
  await db.commit();
  await cache.invalidate(`user:${userId}:pref`);
}
```

